---
import Docs from '../../layouts/Docs.astro';
---

<Docs slug="survey">
      <h2 id="sv-survey">Survey a page</h2>
      <pre class="code"><code>cue survey http://localhost:3000/login</code></pre>
      <p>It opens the page, notes everything you can interact with, and saves it:</p>
      <div class="codegroup">
        <div class="tabs"><span class="filename">.agent-kb/app-map/login.yaml</span></div>
        <pre><code>route: /login
title: Sign in
verifiedAt: 2026-09-10T18:39:26.471Z
elements:
  - role: button
    name: Log in
    locator: "getByRole('button', &#123; name: 'Log in' &#125;)"
    confidence: runtime-only
links:
  - name: Forgot password?
    href: /forgot</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="callout warn"><strong>Warning</strong><p>Point it at a development or staging environment, never production.</p></div>
      <h2 id="sv-lookup">Look things up</h2>
      <pre class="code"><code>cue locator "log in button"</code></pre>
      <p>When there is no entry, Cue refuses and names the command that fills the gap. A tool that guesses here is worse than no tool.</p>
      <h2 id="sv-confidence">Confidence</h2>
      <div class="table"><table>
        <thead><tr><th>Value</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><code>confirmed</code></td><td>In your app's code and seen on the page.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>runtime-only</code></td><td>Seen on the page, not found in your code. It may come from a library and may move.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>code-only</code></td><td>In your code, never seen. It may be dead or behind a feature flag.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table></div>
      <div class="callout note"><strong>Note</strong><p>Commit <code>.agent-kb/</code>. Values that look like passwords, tokens or email addresses are stripped before writing, but read the first commit anyway.</p></div>
    
</Docs>
